.TH "GLESHA-CREATE" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-create \- register a new backup set
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha create\fR SET PATH... [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Register a backup set named SET whose sources are the directories PATH. Each PATH becomes a root named after its last path component. No data is archived; use 'glesha run SET' to create the first snapshot.
.PP
Remotes given with \-\-to become the set's destinations. The catalog is stored on the first of them unless \-\-catalog\-to says otherwise. A set without \-\-to gets its destinations from the first run.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Remote options
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Upload snapshots to REMOTE.
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-to REMOTE|local
Where to keep the catalog (default: the first \-\-to remote).
.PP
REMOTE... takes a comma\-separated list and may be repeated. If \-\-from or \-\-to is given, no other remote is accessed.
.SS Archive options
.TP
.B \-\-storage\-class CLASS
AWS storage class of snapshots.
.TP
.B \-\-compression FORMAT
Compression: xz, gzip, or bzip2 (default: xz).
.TP
.B \-\-compression\-level N
Compression level, 1 to 9 (default: 6).
.TP
.B \-\-prefix PREFIX
Name prefix: glesha or encb (default: glesha).
.TP
.B \-\-incremental\-storage\-class CLASS
AWS storage class of incremental snapshots (default: \-\-storage\-class).
.TP
.B \-\-chunked
Upload in chunks using bounded local space. Chunked snapshots cannot be kept with \-\-output or \-\-keep\-archive, cannot use memory archive mode, cannot be moved with glesha move, and cannot be changed with glesha storage\-class.
.TP
.B \-\-spool\-max SIZE
Local space for chunks (default: 128MiB, min: 2MiB). Requires \-\-chunked.
.SS Passphrase options
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file FILE
Read the catalog passphrase from FILE ('\-': stdin). Without this option, GLESHA_CATALOG_PASSPHRASE or a hidden prompt is used.
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha create docs ~/Documents \-\-to b2
glesha create photos ~/Pictures \-\-to aws \-\-storage\-class DEEP_ARCHIVE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-configure (1),
.BR glesha\-run (1)
